It'd be nice to be able to use something to take brivla that don't have "by
standard xn" places and make a lujvo that has a place like that. For
example, if we were going to make a lujvo for "modern", I think Pierre's
example of "Modern English" suggests that it have a standard place.

For example, we could coin {stana} to mean "x1 is a standard for x2". Not
sure if we would want to fragment this depending on the epistemological
context, but this would be an easy enough hack for the time being.

mu'o mi'e .latros.

